From 8847ef602682f07a81be9f0653b0c306b0450fa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincent <vincent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:42:33 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a parallel tool exchange split for DeepSeek's
 Messages API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DeepSeek's Anthropic-format API turns a parallel tool exchange away —
one assistant message with several tool_use blocks answered by the
tool_result blocks of the next user message, the shape Claude Code
sends for parallel tool calls — with 400 "tool_use ids were found
without tool_result blocks immediately after …", although Anthropic's
own API takes it and DeepSeek's Chat API does too (so sequential tool
calls through magpie worked, and a direct Chat-path bypass too, while
every parallel-call turn failed: #4945). Its own tracker has the same
refusal from the raw Anthropic SDK (deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3#967), so
no translation of ours caused it: the endpoint takes the calls one
assistant message at a time.

A Messages request relayed (passthrough) or translated to a Messages
upstream that wants a turn's thinking back — anthropicReplaysThinking,
the same gate withThinkingOnToolTurns runs under — now has each
parallel exchange split into the sequential ones that endpoint answers
(splitParallelToolUses): one call an assistant message, its result the
user message after it, what the user said beside the results after the
last of them. An exchange of one call, or one the next message doesn't
fully answer, goes as it was; a body with nothing to split comes back
byte for byte. Claude's own API keeps the parallel exchange, and so
does any other Messages upstream.

Evidence: TestMessagesParallelToolUsesSplitForDeepSeekUpstream (a
Messages relay to an upstream refusing parallel exchanges with
DeepSeek's own words fails on main, answers 200 with the split),
TestTranslatedMessagesParallelToolUsesSplitForDeepSeek and
TestSplitParallelToolUsesOnARelayedBody (results out of order, text
beside them, one-call and unanswered exchanges untouched). Not tried:
a real api.deepseek.com/anthropic request; the endpoint's refusal and
its acceptance of the sequential shape are taken from its own issue
tracker, where the raw SDK reproduces both.
